(Thus far, we have dealt with Boolean queries: a document either matches or does) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 666.0 Td
(not match a query. For large collections, a Boolean query often results in either) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 650.5 Td
(too few or too many thousands of results. It takes skill to craft a Boolean query) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 635.0 Td
(that produces a manageable number of hits. Consequently, it is far more desirable) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 619.5 Td
(to compute a numeric score between 0 and 1 for each document that measures how) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 604.0 Td
(well document and query match.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
68 580.5 Td
(How do we assign a weight to a term in a document? First, the term frequency tf\(t,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 565.0 Td
(d\) is the number of occurrences of term t in document d. However, raw frequency) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 549.5 Td
(alone treats common words that appear in almost every document as equally) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 534.0 Td
(discriminative as rare terms. Therefore, we attenuate the effect of terms that) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 518.5 Td
(occur too often in the collection by scaling with inverse document frequency:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 503.0 Td
(idf\(t\) = log\(N / df\(t\)\), where N is the total number of documents and df\(t\) is the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 487.5 Td
(number of documents containing term t.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
68 464.0 Td
(Combining these two quantities yields the tf-idf weight: w\(t, d\) = tf\(t, d\) ×) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 448.5 Td
(idf\(t\). The tf-idf weight of a term is highest when t occurs many times within a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 433.0 Td
(small number of documents, lending high discriminating power to those documents.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
68 409.5 Td
(In the vector space model, each document d is viewed as a vector with one) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 394.0 Td
(component in the dictionary for each term, weighted by its tf-idf value. To) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 378.5 Td
(compensate for the effect of document length, we quantify the similarity between) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 363.0 Td
(two documents -- or between a query q and a document d -- as the cosine of the angle) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 347.5 Td
(between their length-normalized vectors.) Tj
ET
